# Messaging and resilience

- **Kafka:** Event DTOs must be **Jackson-serializable** (constructors/setters as needed for consumers). Publishing fits the existing checkout/event flow unless designing a new pattern (document in ARCHITECTURE if so).
- **Resilience4j:** Keep circuit breaker / retry / limits on **external-style** boundaries (e.g. payment gateway), consistent with **application.yml** instance names.
- **Checkout:** Do **not** “fix” failures by moving payment to **`REQUIRES_NEW`** without an explicit outbox/saga-style design — it can break FK visibility vs the order transaction (see ARCHITECTURE).
- **Inventory:** Respect **`@Version`** and existing **`@Retryable`** behavior on optimistic lock conflicts.

See **ARCHITECTURE.md** (“Transactions and consistency”, “Messaging”, “Resilience”).
